# Model endpoint for round-1 grading and round-2 re-examination.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the key. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so keep secrets
# out of it. Everything here is read by `backend/dotenv.py` and by the Makefile, and anything
# already exported in your shell wins over the file.
#
# Endpoints from the organisers' post (AMD MI300X):
# https://discuss.flower.ai/t/collaborative-agent-hackathon-cambridge-uk-2026/1269
#
#   | model          | endpoint                                  | model id                       | key   |
#   |----------------|-------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|-------|
#   | GLM-5.2        | http://129.212.179.194:8001/v1/responses  | glm-5.2-fp8                    | Slack |
#   | Qwen3.5 397B   | http://129.212.182.232:8001/v1/responses   | /models/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-FP8  | none  |
#   | Kimi-K2.7-Code | http://134.199.193.245:8001/v1/responses   | /models/Kimi-K2.7-Code         | Slack |
#   | MiniMax-M3     | http://165.245.135.52:8001/v1/responses    | minimax-m3                     | Slack |
#
# Keys are posted in #hackathon_cambridge_2026. Qwen takes none — leave the key blank for it,
# which `dotenv.load` reads as "unset" rather than sending an empty Bearer header.
#
# Switching model invalidates the on-disk cache: the fingerprint covers the model id, so the
# first run on a new model pays full latency on every call.

FLWR_MODEL_API_ENDPOINT=http://129.212.179.194:8001/v1/responses
CONSORTIUM_MODEL=glm-5.2-fp8
FLWR_MODEL_API_KEY=
